e dropped out well if you weren't  already with Bernie then Pete dropping  out more than likely pushes you to Joe  by  if Amy drops out which she did and  endorses Joe Biden well that's more  support for Joe Biden so the question  was is there a significant amount of the  support for other candidates Pete and  Amy as an example that would go to  Bernie Sanders or is Biden going to get  the lion's share of Amy and Pete's  supporters does a big rally with Amy and  Beto O'Rourke gets the Pete endorsement  and then they get the results they want  on Super Tuesday with Biden even winning  some states outright like Texas and  Minnesota where he was supposed to lose  he was going to get delegates but he was  supposed to lose those states so now  there's all sorts of enlightened  analyses coming out of the woodwork you  know the DNC establishment stole it  Bernie's campaign was ganged up on it  was voter suppression insiders don't  want Bernie to be the nominee corporate  media has been boosting Biden and  hurting Bernie all along and every  single one of those has some truth to it  there is no question but we also have to  realize that bernie is not merely the  victim here because if we don't  recognize that the progressive movement  will never win and that would be a  tragedy when we see Bernie not take PAC  money we love it it's the right thing to  do it's morally correct  lots of House seats have been won in  that way but every decision has some  risk associated with it when Bernie  doesn't play these inside baseball party  politics games with the Democratic Party  where they coordinate they say let's get  Pete out let's figure out how to stop  this cannon let's get Bernie out on this  day get a me out on this state to  endorse I love that Bernie doesn't play  those games he just runs his campaigns  he tells it like he sees it he says what  he would do he puts together policy  Bernie is loved because he doesn't play  those games but in a lot of the real  world sometimes you need to play those  games to get into a position of power in  the first place to then change the  system so when we say the establishment  stole it there's no doubt the DNC  establishment coordinated this 96-hour  plan of consolidating Amy and Budaj edge  around a Joe Biden of course it was  fabricated and planned but it only works  if there's enough centrist or  center-left support to make it possible  and it was so we have to  recognize that when we spend time on  Twitter and reddit we get an overly  optimistic assessment of the portion of  the National Democratic a letter  electorate who wants someone like Bernie  that's not an attack on Bernie there's  lots of candidates that are liked excuse  me getting very fired up and punching my  Mike there's lots of candidates that are  liked and disliked by different  electorates it doesn't tell us if  they're good or bad candidates but we  have to recognize that if you ask people  about Medicare for all people are  increasingly for it you ask people about  free college people are increasingly for  it there are lots of people who don't  want Bernie to be the nominee and a lot  of them voted last night when so many  people come out and vote for someone  other than Bernie we can't just say  people are confused and they were  tricked by the DNC and bla bla bla bla  bla because then we will not win if  that's what we do if we just say we are  the victims and everybody else's has  either been bamboozled or whatever the  case may be when you look at people  supporting Biden Pete and Amy throughout  the campaign and not going to Bernie we  tried to ignore it but there is this  total amount of center-left ideology in  the Democratic Party Medicare for all  more popular than ever free college you  zoom out and there are millions of  Democrats who believe in what they call  capitalism and they hear democratic  socialism and they don't like it  socialism viewed more favorably now than  in decades but there are lots of  Democratic primary voters who believe in  what they see as moderation this is not  an attack on anybody this is not praise  for anybody  it's assessing the electorate Bernie bet  on a ton of new voters that he could  bring out but new voters voted by  roughly the same proportion as in 2016  in some states lower new voter turnout  there is a race at racial analysis to be  made Bernie one Hispanic voters with 50%  he only got 15 percent of the black vote  yesterday 60% four by Biden young voters  a lot stayed home another group Bernie  was counting on and then lastly there is  something to be said just more broadly  about coalition's and the people that  different  candidates get involved with and sort of  the the note that that the chord that  that strikes with a more casual follower  of politics I've talked about some of  the toxic people around Bernie I can see  past it because I care about policy and  I believe Bernie has the right policies  but all over my facebook page and  Twitter account  there were people telling me you know  David I agree with Bernie the most every  time I do one of these tests about whose  policy is closest to yours but I don't  want to implicitly approve of the toxic  people Bernie has around him and they  said so I ended up voting for Biden so  if you said to me well how could Bernie  have fixed it that would require me to  tell you that Bernie should have been  someone other than who he is the last  thing I'm going to tell you is Bernie  should be inauthentic because bernie is  all about authenticity  he calls himself a Democratic Socialist  he has the people around him that he  wants around him Bernie refuses to do  the inauthentic stuff and this was the  result okay  tons of people have been saying Bernie  needs a one-on-one against someone else  in the primary and then he'll do really  well it became very quickly a de facto  one-on-one of course Bloomberg taking  votes from Biden and Warren likely  taking votes from Bernie we now have to  go 